    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2849e77c_cc02828e",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-20T22:20:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(Note that authfs and fd_server are already under com.android.virt / in the pKVM apex.)\n\nYeah, we just need a clear interface.  On the client side, it needs to pass the fd to fd_server, then send the \"annotations\" to the server; on the server side, it needs to start authfs given the annotations.  These are essentially what pvm_exec and compsvc_worker do (besides parsing the command line arguments).  We could turn them into some stable libraries to ship in pKVM apex.  Any suggestions?",
      "parentUuid": "922241ca_76af6875",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e906f24_033802b6",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-22T18:07:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s figure out the details later.  For now, I think this component is probably generic enough, and we could put it in com.android.virt.apex.  I\u0027d rename the directory name to compsvc as well.  David, WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "2849e77c_cc02828e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01ae6161_0d8e777b",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T22:39:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry Victor but I do have reservations to encouraging users to build pVMs with a command line API. There may be reasons why to do it for dex2oat but we should encourage users to write a proper AIDL, build a Binder service that implements it and then give them tools that automagically help them set up the FD sharing. And once we figure out how to integrate authfs into libbinder, it will be easy to remove the magic. I know it\u0027s more work for you but would you mind splitting this up?",
      "parentUuid": "3e906f24_033802b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df80319e_9a9ed2c0",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T23:38:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do like a binder better than a command line as a developer API, at least it feels more like a service that can be potentially accessed by anyone (my main reservation of the developer API in general is that it\u0027s not clear what we\u0027re going to tell the developers about, such as that their code in the VM can\u0027t trust their own code from the other side.  An API can inject/imply false assumption easily.).\n\nFor compos, this is already working.  I just thought this can be reused for \"executing a binary from an app inside microdroid\".  But it doesn\u0027t have to be if we think there will be a different way later.  If binder can indeed support transparent CD passing, then the developer\u0027s executable could just be an init argument (though they might need some work to run multiple executables).  It\u0027s going to take a long time to achieve that, I think.  Steven and I should talk more about the setup to make FD passing transparent.  For now, I think it\u0027s better to land this as is.",
      "parentUuid": "01ae6161_0d8e777b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e447773_a6656341",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-27T12:28:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately it is the case that VMs cannot trust any external entity, that is just a fact of the matter, and we\u0027ll have to communicate that to users. And nudging them towards the client-server model of AIDL is the way to help them make the right decisions. So I am sorry but I don\u0027t want to land this as is.\n\nI also don\u0027t think that transparent FD passing is a prerequisite - we can expose the Input/OutputFd structs for use in the AIDL interfaces together with libraries for setting authfs up on both ends.",
      "parentUuid": "df80319e_9a9ed2c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82d378a6_00d3fd60",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-27T17:25:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this change itself has nothing to do with the developers, and why it should be blocked.  But I understand the desire to split the common utilities here.\n\nI do think we need to know what the final architecture of FD passing will look like, before starting any refactoring here.  There are many components/roles/privileges to consider in such architecture, and I\u0027d like to get aligned first.",
      "parentUuid": "1e447773_a6656341",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e8441a9_326c3b0e",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
