        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-20T22:20:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Output size can be arbitrary.\n\nFor input files, they are supposed to be read-only, and will be verified against fs-verity hash algorithm.  IIRC, size (and stat in general) is needed during the lookup of each FUSE entry.  And for fs-verity verification, we need the size to correctly walk the Merkle tree.\n\nTechnically, we could query the size on demand of each file, but in the current use cases, that only seems to complicate things.",
      "parentUuid": "d0fd867e_7000b9c3",
      "revId": "f5400c8a87f3eb181dc7a8564576302dc472a965",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
